{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbTJCERmC4rmFnpeMGY8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote candidate `run_length_variety_encoding`, and the self-check printed `OK`. That check only ran one short chain (100 draws), so convergence and novelty against the other models haven't been tested yet; admission's full fit will do that.\n\n**Hypothesis.** People hold a sequence in working memory as a list of runs (stretches of identical flips). If every run is the same length, as in strict alternation (HTHTHTHT) or pairs (HHTTHHTT), the list boils down to one repeated chunk size, so the sequence looks made by a rule and less random. A mix of short and longer runs looks random.\n\n**Model.** It keeps all of the current best model, `individual_alternation_sensitivity_mirror`, and adds one term:\n- **New feature:** run-length variety, which is the number of distinct run lengths, scaled by the most a sequence of that length could have.\n- **New parameter:** one shared weight on that feature, `omega`, with a Normal(0, 1.5) prior.\n\nThis targets one of the two critique results that held up after the false-discovery correction. Among pairs with the same alternation rate, people picked the sequence with more distinct run lengths 0.706 of the time; the current best model predicts 0.624.\n\n**Check results:**\n- The short fit's ELPD-LOO was −2273.5, against the best model's −2301.4 from a full fit. With so short a fit that is only a rough sign of improvement, not a valid comparison.\n- PSIS-LOO came out unreliable on the short fit: 6.7% of trials had a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance. The full fit may or may not clear that.\n\n**Possible problem:** I didn't address the other critique result. People choose the more alternating sequence in high-alternation pairs more often than the model predicts, and this new term could make that slightly worse, because strict alternation has only one run length and so counts as low variety.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_1/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2639,"cache_read_input_tokens":71136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2639,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"689da2fe-b76a-4d39-b741-acf6d52555b2","uuid":"f8cf6cc9-d210-46a7-b6b1-c12ddd87a992","timestamp":"2026-10-01T11:40:38.060Z","request_id":"req_011CfbTJBneEynm1fDyz8Ukv"}
